{"author":{"id":"249c5793827ca0939286dfdbd6c35d9aabfb778e27ec8eab6c06481033d4a9ab"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792313460,"nonce":"xbqgpERuXmEY9IlCz3ge8Zjt5ao=","title":"The web build ships in the Haxelib ZIP and a wasm build stages it","message":"The wasm build was a separate release zip, `hlwindow-wasm-ash.zip`, and a program built for a page had to collect its files by hand. A build defined `wasm` with `-lib hlwindow` should have them beside its output without a Rust toolchain, as a desktop build has its hdll.\n\n**Done**\n\n- `scripts/package_haxelib.py --web \u003cdirectory\u003e` puts xwindow.wasm, xwindow.mjs and xwindow_wire.mjs in the ZIP under `web/`, and stops the release when one is missing; the release workflow passes the wasm job's artifact.\n- `hlwindow.macro.NativeInstall` copies them beside the output of a build defined `wasm`, in place of the host library. `-D hlwindow_web=\u003cdirectory\u003e` names another directory, for a checkout whose web build is in `target`.\n\n**Context**\n\nashui's page build stages its own page and `blinc_abi.wasm`; with these, a web build of an app needs no step but the Haxe compile and `ash --build`.","files":null}]}